        "identifier": "EPE_1926032501",
        "title": "Empress express (1926-03-25)",
        "creator": null,
        "archival_reference": null,
        "specialist_agent": null,
        "description": "Page 1: - United Church - Local News - Golf Club Hold Meeting - Irish Tea - Bindloss W. I. - File Oil Leases at Steveville - Farm Probe Meeting - Anglican Church Page 2: - Suppression of Crime - Columbus of the Air - Big Salmon Pack - Local News - Local News - Would Ban This Royal Sport - Through Service for Steamship Passengers - The More the Merrie - What Canad Offers - Local News - Local News - A Curious Occupation - Beatty May Succeed Byng - Cannot Export Electric Energy - Prince is Real Sport - Use Armored Car - Contains Priceless Pictures - Boy Astounds Scientists Page 3: - Gradual Reorganization of King Cabinet Said to be Contemplated - Channel Islands Should Pay - Dominions May be Represented - Britain Will Do Nothing to Jeopardize Results of the Locarno Treaty - Last Week in the Alberta Legislature - Executed by Reds - Plan for Forest Fire Protection - Appeals to Privy Council - For Corporal Punishment - Claims Prohibition Law Was Violated - Russia Liberates Prisoners - Poet Visits Winter Carnival - Germany Hears About War-Time Conditions - One New Membership for League Council - Reports Are Encouraging - Urges Reduction of Canada's Gold Reserve - Plane Carries First Red Lake Passenger - Making Use of lce Bridge - Entertained Distinguished Guest - Progressives Will Co-Operate Openly With the Government - Rural Credits Measure and Pension Bill to Come before Houes - Lady Astor Willing to Resign - Fast Mail Service for Victoria - Germany Extends Credit to Russia Page 4: - Seed Grain for Argentine - Jay Gould's Invention - Juvenile Crime - Convicted on His Own Evideence - Scott Was Her Favorite - Local News - Chimney Fires - Railroad Men Have Picturesque Dialect - Weymouth People Long-Lied - Fower Pecple in Tropics - Canadian Wolf is Fierce - Proves Wooden Ships Seaworthy Many Years - About Birthdays - Where Money Talks - The Canadian Flag on Mediterranean Tour - Suitalbe for Flax Growing - Was Record Performance - Capt. Cook's Voyages - New Zealand Likes Canadians - Local News - Science Indebted to Primitive Medicine Men - Arabic Women Independent - Aeropiane is Popular Goods Carrier - Local News - Wins Success in Alberta - Jack Miner, the Bird Lover - Notice Came Too Late - Local News Page 5: - Fur Farming Industry in All Its Branches is Now Firmly Established in Canads - To Protect Teachers - Wintered Largest Herd in Canada - Start Dog Farm - \"Clan Donald\" Colonists - Our Export Trade - Wants to Loven up World - local News - Local News - Canada's Rubber Trade - Wheat Exports - Pure-Bred Stock - New Danish Air Service - Special Features on C. N.R. Broadcasts - Investigate Quality of Wheat - To Erect New Canneries - Build Large Saw Mill - Has Confidence in World Court - Will Raise Muskrats on Extensive Scale - Canada's Egg Output - Local News - United States Navy Plans for Great Aerial Dreadnaughts Bristling with Heavy Guns - Settlers Coming from Britain - Makes Good Windbreaks - Wheat to be Shipped West - Will Raise Muskrats Page 6: - World Happenings Briefly Told - Repudiates Fascist Government - Unto the End - Another Game Reserve - Was Nephew of Livingstone - Has to Abandon Plan - Colony of Hungarian Nobility - A New Oil Industry - Would be Unusual Case - Is a Lie Ever Justified - New Lieut-Governor of B. C. - Germany's Industrial Situation - On the Air - Woman Leaves Three Millions for Animals - Canada's Electric Power Development - Buys Famous Blacksmith Shop - Local News - A Stabilized Easter - Old Letter Discovered - Soviets Will Not Enter Switzerland - Saving Huge Sums - An Expensive Business - Change in Direction of Japanese Current - Good Honey Customers - Local News Page 7: - Baree, Son of Kazan - Local News - Local News - Bears Acted as Judges - Soviet Reviews Reds' Fate - Name Restricted Area - Common Cold is Dangerous - Admiral Togo Excepted - Lethbridge Northern Irrigation District - Local News - Little Helps for This Week - Trans-Canada Highway Page 8: - Local News - A Free Gift with Reservations - Minutes R. M. Mantario February 27th Meeting",
