      {
        "identifier": "celticbookoflivi0000wood",
        "title": "The Celtic book of living and dying : the illustrated guide to Celtic wisdom",
        "creator": "Wood, Juliette",
        "archival_reference": null,
        "specialist_agent": null,
        "description": [
          "144 pages : 25 cm",
          "The Celts were a dynamic and unique people who left not only a rich legacy of artistic treasures, but also a vast body of wisdom and mystical symbolism that reflects universal truths about life",
          "Includes bibliographical references and index",
          "An eagle's flight. The wise child ; The warrior's way ; The honour of women ; Last things ; This was the house -- The wheel of nature. Two faces : growth and decay ; The wisdom of the weather ; The wisdom of the seasons ; The sun and the moon -- Echoes of the Otherworld. The islands beyond ; Impossibilities ; Veils of illusion ; Mystical creatures ; Talismans of power ; Fairy mounds -- Voyages between realms. The threshold of the beyond ; The enchanted archipelago ; Visions of our ancestor ; The wisdom of water ; Vessels of truth ; In the guise of a swan -- Fate and foreknowledge. Our yesterdays are our tomorrows ; The wisdom of the salmon ; The mystery of the head ; Birds of destruction -- Guardians of the soul. The wisdom of the Druids ; Magical contest ; The fortress of love ; The wisdom of inspiration ; Saints and angels ; The power of three ; Spiritual healing ; The wisdom of the bards -- The wisdom of eternity. The creatures in the pattern ; The twisted vine ; The endless knot ; The great bard ; How to live, how to die"
        ],
        "subject": [
          "Celts -- Religion",
          "Wisdom -- Religious aspects",
          "Mythology, Celtic"
        ],
