      {
        "identifier": "furcamp-2026-conbook",
        "title": "FURCAMP 2026 - Conbook",
        "creator": "FURCAMP",
        "archival_reference": null,
        "specialist_agent": null,
        "description": "FURCAMP 2026 was held in São Paulo, Brazil, on February 13–17, 2026. The theme is The Corsairs Legacy. The materials included here were originally distributed to convention attendees and are being shared strictly for purposes of historical preservation purposes. This presentation constitutes fair use under Section 107 of the U.S. Copyright Act, as it is transformative and does not substitute for or diminish the market value of the original materials, especially ones that were shared publically to all attendees. FURCAMP is an annual furry event created in Brazil, held every year around mid-February or mid-March, during the Brazilian Carnival season. Unlike traditional conventions, FURCAMP offers a unique camping-style experience, bringing the community closer to nature. The event takes place in a large outdoor area, with accommodation options including cozy lodges and tent camping, allowing attendees to choose how immersed they want to be in the environment. Surrounded by nature, FURCAMP blends the spirit of adventure with the warmth of the furry fandom. Over the course of five unforgettable days, participants can enjoy a wide variety of activities, from games and social gatherings to themed events and moments of pure relaxation. Between exploring the natural surroundings and connecting with fellow attendees, it quickly becomes clear that five days barely feel like enough to experience everything FURCAMP has to offer. FURCAMP is more than just an event — it’s a shared journey, a place to make memories, friendships, and truly disconnect from everyday life. Convention booklets (conbooks) are creative works that may be protected by copyright. The Furry Con Archive respects the rights of copyright holders while working to preserve these important historical documents for the furry community.",
