      {
        "identifier": "https://openalex.org/W1758439533",
        "title": "War for Profit: Macroculture, Corsairs and partnership companies",
        "creator": [
          "Nicholas C. Kyriazis",
          "Theodore Metaxas"
        ],
        "archival_reference": null,
        "specialist_agent": "contradiction",
        "description": "In the present paper we propose that in states with relatively weak central\\nauthorities, decision makers had to develop market oriented organisation solutions to\\nsuccessfully face a grave external threat, and these solutions proved to be efficient.\\nUsing an interdisciplinary approach that combines institutional theory, history\\nand strategy, we analyse the concept of macroculture and then a case study, the use of\\ncorsairs (privateers) by England and the United Provinces (Dutch Republic) in the late\\n16th and early 17th centuries. We also propose that the development of partnership\\ncompanies went hand in hand for commercial and military purposes.\\nLastly, we suggest that a market led decentralised type of war as practiced by\\nEnglish and Dutch privateers proved to be economically efficient and superior to the\\ncentrally planed war operations of the Spanish empire.",
        "subject": null,
        "context_excerpt": null,
        "mediatype": null,
