        "identifier": "cia-readingroom-document-cia-rdp82-00457r008800570005-2",
        "title": "CIA Reading Room cia-rdp82-00457r008800570005-2: 1. CHINESE COMMUNIST AIR ACTIVITIES 2. SOVIET MILITARY PERSONNEL, CANTON",
        "creator": "CIA Reading Room",
        "archival_reference": null,
        "specialist_agent": null,
        "description": "COUNTRY Approved For Releas CLASSIFICATI CENTRAL INTELLIGENCE AGENCY China 1NFOR ATION EPOT SECURITY INFORMATION SUBJECT la Chinese Communist Air Activities 2. Soviet Military personnel, Canton? ' PLACE 25X1 ACQUIRED DATE OF INFO. 7 'i.,2 li t: '? j L'..41 DO NOT CIRCULATE DATE DISTR. NO. OF PAGES NO. OF ENCLS. (LISTED DELOW) SUPPLEMENT TO REPORT NO. I. Cotq, 1951 2 25X1 IMMOWSITIT CORSAIRS IRFORIJAY3011 ilPirCCTITIGTOP, IINSIORA1L [ARROW OF vor.r. EIMITII0 EMUSWt1TWIG REAM= OP TOO ESPIORAIM ACT SO U. LI, C.. 811 MD 82. AS MUMMA. ITS ITUIRSIOISSIOR OR ICE IMYCIATIO0 OF ITS COMMITS 10 AM HAREMS TO AU WIASTRORSZSO MOON 11;g PRO. OW CR LAM, REPtiOSUCTIOII OP Two PORN IS 051010/1111W-VELIMITrMinre4147' *Except as noted THIS IS UNEVALUATED INFORMATION 25X1 25X1 1. By 19 September Soviet and Chinese mechanics at Mite Cloud Airfield had as-sembled 49 jet fighters. Crates containing unassembled aircraft were continu-ously arriving at Canton by rail from Central China. Assembled planes were tested in the early morning by Manchurian pilots, trained in the USSR. Some of these aircraft are to be assigned to airfields at Swatow, Shaokuan? Hainan, and possibly to fields in Kwangsi. 25X1 2. In mid-September 105 Soviet military experts arrived at Canton and were billeted in the Oilman and bite Hobs? Hotels, Shameen. These Soviets were destined for assigmaents with military establishments and high level units to map out military plans with emphasis on coastal defense. 25X1 25X1 3. A Chinese Jac, recently fled to Canton was told that appro am e 500 bottles of milk per day were supplied to boviets, in-cluding women and children, in Canton. 4. an 15 September, 120 crates were shipped in 3 railway cars from 25X1 enampoa to bnaho 4,1) )? near Tienho Airfield. The crates were apparently unloaded at shampoa from ships from Vladivostok or Dairen and were believed to contain aircraft and spare parts from the USSR. 5. Approximately 50,000 laborers have completed the enlarging of Henning Airfield by one-third its original size. The new construction includes a cement runway one motor thick and several new buildings, including works 'ops and barracks. STATE NAVY CLASSIFICATION S X liSRD ARMY X MR x nu Approved For Releas SEE REVERSE FOR DECLIS'ST1 2 r DISTRIBUTION CINCFE /,' 174A21, C0i'.ThJAVF7 CO liF*,r c0il7 1' CTITCP471Z /,' 8/12 SECURITY INFORMATION 008800570005-2 25X1 25X1 It* Approved For Release 2003/08/12 : CIA-RDP82-00457R008800570005-2 normmni Cz El, Mtn.: Date: tiP Approved For Release 2003/08/12 : CIA-RDP82-00457R008800570005-2 se 2003/08/12 : CIA-RDP82-00457R008800 25X1 Approv el CENTRAL INTELLIGENCE AGENCY -2.. 570005-2 25X1 25X1 6. Chinese Communist practice air maneuvers, in preparation for the celebration of a Chinese Communist national hcliday on 1 October, were to be held in late September by the Chinese Communist Air Pierce (CCAF) at Nanyuan Airfield, in the Peiping area. During these practice maneuvers no other planes were to be per-mitted to land' or take off from this field. 7. On 18 September CCAF activities were as follows: a. One C-46 of the East China Air Transport Unit left Nanking for PeipPg via Hsuchou and Tsinan. The plane was piloted It returned to Nanking on the same day. b. Training missionain (1) T'angshan: a number of MIG-15's and 4 TU-2's. (2) Tsingtao: 21 MI0-15's and one YAK-17 of the CCAF 46 Air Regiment, and a number of MIG-15's of the 48 Air Regiments* On 18 September Soviet Air Force (SAF) training mission from Anshan were as follows: a. 16 MIG-15's and 2 /AK-171s? b. 18 MIG-15's and one YAK-11 c. One LA-11 to Antung and back to Anshan during the night. 9. On 19 September OCAF activities were as felleve: a. A total of le? MIG-15's left Antung and Tatungkou for combat missions in Korea. b. Training missions: (1) Shanghai: 2 fighters. (2) Ch'uelashan: (114-04, 32-49): one 1L-12. 10* On 19 September SAF activities were as follows: a. 20 MIG-15's left Mukden with as flight leader on along distance training mission. b. Two IL-12's left the Pert Arthur-Dairen area for Vladivostok via Mukden. c. Three LI-2's left Voroshilov for Port Arthur with 25X1 25X1 11. On 20 September two CCAF fighters 41new a training mission from Shanghai? 25X1 25X1 25X1 12. On 21 September CCAF activities were as follows: a. Antung: 20 MIG-15's left for oembat missions in Korea. b. Chohsien: 2 LA-5's left for Mukden via Chinchou. c. Training missions: (1) T'angshan: 28 TU-2's and 2 Lk-als. (2) Yangtslun: 21 MIG-151s, (3) Tsingtao: a number of MIG-15\"s of the 46 Air Regiments and 19 MIG-15's and one 111K-17 of the 48 Air Regiment. 13. 25X1 On 21 September 22 MIG-15's and 2 YAK-11's of hiltet SacK:1117 training missions from Kungchuling CORTgo- e 2003/08/12 : CIA-RDP82-00457R 00570005-'2 25X1",
