        "source_text_sha256": "19c55bfa97af33a51960ccd4a626fb5f63bf82a265383326891077fccf9de0a0",
        "evidence_excerpt": "45, ibid., 885.\n46. \" .. ,he (Paolo Somma) wanted to do so much harm [0 the Christians that an angel WQuld corne down from heaven, call him by his renegade name,\n. and urge hiJrno stop ... \", AIM Crim., vo1.59A case 736, ff. 67v~6S, 1O,xU645,\n47. Nevertheless free Christian and Jewish subjects, with a V'dlid licence continued to travel on their awn business throughout the Medilerranean at a\ntime when corsairing actiYities were at their best. In 1645 Giovanni Maria dell' Alberi of Vittoriosa explained [hat he had rravelled to TUllis in March\nof that year and returned in Augt,lst He also referred to a free Jew of run is who was in Malta at th·at time. Naturally the Jews. like other minorities\nwithin (he Olloman Empire such as the Armenians and the Greeks, served as middlemen in formal exchange of trade between Christians and\nMuslims. AThl Crim., v01.59A case 736, [67. 19.xl,l645.\n.\n48. J. M. Abun-~asr, A History of the Maghrib in the Islamic Peried, (Cambridge. 1937), 159.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1645
        ],
