        "evidence_excerpt": "Toward the year 67 B.c. the forays of the pirates were \nbecoming too bold even for the sea-hating Romans to \nsuffer them in patience any longer. The pirates, indeed, \nattacked them in their most vulnerable part—their food- \nsupply. A bad season came, when the cornfields of Italy \nwere struck by blight and disease. At the same time the \nexpected corn-ships from Egypt did not arrive, and soon \nit was learned that the bags of golden grain which had",
