        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Pompey had twenty-four lieutenants under him, \ntogether with a hundred and twenty thousand foot- \nsoldiers and five thousand cavalry. Assembling his \nlieutenants at Brundisium, where the main part of the \ngreat fleet was assembled, he laid his plans before them. \nEach man was to have a certain number of galleys under \nhim, and with these he was to keep within a certain area \nof the Mediterranean, and in that area he was to search \nout and destroy every pirate stronghold and to burn or \nscuttle every galley belonging to the corsairs. There \nwere thirteen of these divisions, which as the pirates soon \nfound, were like the meshes of a great net, for if they fled \nout of one, they fell into another.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
