        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "As he walked slowly homeward Elphin sadly reflected, \nand things became a little plainer to him. Seven years \nbefore, when Elphin was a little fellow of ten, playing \nbefore his home in a narrow lane of the castrum, he had \nseen his father coming toward him, leading a strange \nlittle boy by the hand—a boy with a mass of blond curls, \nwith sullen, fierce blue eyes, dressed in woollen tunic, \nbreeches, and sea-boots, like one of the pirates whom \nElphin had seen once or twice hanging on a cross by the \nwayside outside the fort. His father had had a strange \ntale to tell.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
