      {
        "finding_id": "section-09cc92c9eef478fab871",
        "file": "bookofpirates0000gilb_bookofpirates0000gilb_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The book of pirates",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/bookofpirates0000gilb",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Gilbert, Henry, 1868-1937",
          "date": [
            "1916-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "fighting. By their dress both appeared to be pirates, \nand they hacked and thrust at each other savagely \namong the bushes. Evidently they were making for the \ncreek. In order not to be cut off, and to warn his own \nmen, lest the pagans were in great force, Elphin fled back \nto the galley, and, reaching it, was about to jump aboard \nand order the rowers to push off, when a fierce struggling \nin the bushes behind him drew his attention. He turned \nto see the two Saxons in desperate combat on the water’s \nedge. One was a big, tall man, bareheaded, with an \nevil-looking face—more evil-looking from the fact that \nhe had shaved off all the hair of his head, and had deep \nblue signs tattooed on cheeks and forehead ; moreover \nhis teeth had been filed so that each ended in a point, and \nthey were all coloured blue. His opponent was a slighter \nand a younger man, whose fair hair rolled from beneath the \nedge of his bronze headpiece. The younger man’s \nstrength was evidently no match for his enemy’s, for the \nfierce blows of the bald man’s axe on the other’s bronze \nbuckler made him stagger.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/bookofpirates0000gilb",
          "source_file": "bookofpirates0000gilb_bookofpirates0000gilb_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 101500,
          "end_char": 102599,
          "start_line": 2831,
          "end_line": 2850,
          "printed_page": null,
          "scan_indexes_0_based": [],
          "pdf_file": null,
          "pdf_reference_base": "LANE_ROOT",
          "original_inspected": false
        },
        "reported_cited_pages": [],
