        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Men sighed and shook their heads as they heard all \nthis news. Was there no general there who had brains \nand energy enough to grasp the situation, gather the \nscattered soldiers, and beat back the insolent barbarians ? \nA little later and the news ran like fire through the land \nthat the Saxon pirates were landing in large numbers, \nwere joining their fellows who had helped the Picts to \nbreak down the Wall, and together they were spreading \nterror, ruin, and death through all the northern districts. \nTroopers, covered with the foam from their panting \nhorses, dashed into Rutupie, Regulbium, Lemanis, and \nDubris with orders from the chief general in the north",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
