        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Soon the British felt that they had the mastery of \ntheir enemy : they were the equal of the pirates in sea- \nmanship and in daring, and they had the quality of dash \nand fire which was lacking in the colder nature of the \nSaxons. Toward the end of the summer of 369 hardly \na pirate craft would show its nose upon the waters of \nthe Northern Sea or in the narrows of the Channel.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
