      },
      {
        "finding_id": "section-1acfa461491563d9fa7e",
        "file": "bookofpirates0000gilb_bookofpirates0000gilb_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The book of pirates",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/bookofpirates0000gilb",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Gilbert, Henry, 1868-1937",
          "date": [
            "1916-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Suddenly there came the cry of a seabird— twee \nwee wee ’’—from behind the huts, and Elphin knew that \nHerro and his men were ready. He whispered swift \ninstructions to the centurions by his side, who crept \nquickly and silently away. In the meantime the Saxons \nwere catching the rest of the fleeing victims and forcing \nthem to the slipway. But now the last were being \ndragged to the place, which soon would be a welter of \ncrushed bodies, when suddenly into the thick of the men \nwho were just getting ready to knock away the wedges \nunder the boats there buzzed a cloud of javelins. At \nthe same moment, with a roar which terrified and con- \nfused the pirates, a body of men seemed to rush upon \nthem from all sides. Taken utterly unawares and",
