        "evidence_excerpt": "in war bands, and where they could they seized land \nin the remoter parts of the north-east coast, between the \nHumber and the Forth, and settled down there with \ncaptured wives or with kinswomen from their homelands. \nThus began those long years of blood-stained history \ncalled the Conquest of Britain by the English, during \nwhich pirate Saxon and half civilized Briton began \nbetween them the creation of the British race as we know \nit to-day.",
