      {
        "finding_id": "section-94b60c09fd913bda24e5",
        "file": "bookofpirates0000gilb_bookofpirates0000gilb_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The book of pirates",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/bookofpirates0000gilb",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Gilbert, Henry, 1868-1937",
          "date": [
            "1916-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "forth had been the capture of the ‘Sea Devil,’ Sidi ben \nMuza. But Sidi had had timely knowledge of the \ndescent to be made upon Oran. Loading up his galleys \nwith his treasure, his harem, and everything of value that \nwas portable, he had fled long before the Spaniard had \ngot under way, and, with his fleet of two dozen galleys, \nhad rowed up the Dardanelles and had laid all before the \nfeet of Bajazet. He was graciously accepted into the \nservice of the Grand Turk, who placed a large fleet under \nhis charge; and then, after he had settled his wives \nand family in a splendid villa overlooking the pleasant \nshores of the Bosporus, the pirate chief had put to \nsea, vowed to wage war upon Spaniard, Venetian, \nGenoan, and Frenchman indifferently. With what \nsuccess he ravaged the shores, captured the vessels, \nenslaved the subjects of each of those nations the \nhistories of the Turkish fleet in the early days of the \nsixteenth century bear full witness. He was known to \nthe Spaniards by the name which denoted his possession \nof Satanic qualities; but to the Venetian and Genoese \nmerchants and military men he was referred to by a \nname which showed that they recognized his elusiveness \nand death-dealing characteristics : to these he was ‘the \nPestilence.’",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
