        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "“Hook their boat to and iron the rascals!’ came \nthe command in a high, well-bred voice from the forecastle \nor rambades. Great boat-hooks leaped out and held \nthe brigantine as in the grip of a vice. Each pirate was \ndragged aboard the vessel, and the smiths stood ready with \nshackles, which they clipped upon the wrists of the \ncaptives. Then, with a run, the prisoners.were forced \nalong the gang-plank and down a scuttle into the hold. \nHere they would have to stay until they were needed \nto take their places on the rowing benches. There were \nothers in the dark hold: several Moslem villagers who \nhad recently been captured, and a few seamen who had \nbeen taken off a trading-boat. One who lay where Uruj \nhad been flung had been wounded in a scuffle and lay \ngroaning.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
