        "evidence_excerpt": "Soon after this a party of Moslems landed at Jigelli \nand craved audience of Uruj. They were an embassy \nfrom Algiers, where, for six years now, the Spaniards \nhad held down the pirates, dominating the town from \nthe strong fortress called the Pefion, which they had built \nat the mouth of the harbour. Algiers was one of the \nprincipal cities of refuge to which the Moors of Spain \nhad fled, where knight and artisan, once ejected from their \nhomes in Spain, had banded together to prey upon the \nships of Spain in revenge for the miseries they and their \nforbears had endured. So successful had been the",
