        "evidence_excerpt": "many of whom were proud of their descent from the \ngreat families of Moorish kings and princes. Black looks \nand fierce glances began to take the place of smiling friend- \nliness ; the’sheikh Salim, indeed, was even less discreet, and \nbegan to talk loudly and to threaten. When, therefore, one \nday the news was bruited abroad that Salim had been \nstrangled in his bath by order of Uruj, the Algerine \nnotables and the kinsmen of Salim saw that there was \nno hope for them unless they took instant and active \nmeasures to put an end to the despotic corsair’s power.",
