        "evidence_excerpt": "the very elements betrayed His Most Catholic Majesty \nand heavy autumnal gales put confusion into the Spanish \narmy and destroyed a hundred and fifty ships. The \nattempt ended in tragedy, and, chased and scattered \nby renewed tempests, the remains of the Spanish fleet \nstaggered home, leaving Algiers more defiant than ever. \nOnly with the battle of-Lepanto in 1571, when the \nTurkish fleet was annihilated; was a supreme blow struck \nat the corsairs ; but the Christian Powers did not follow \nup their success, and Algiers continued to be the chief \nof numerous nests of pirates along the shores of Northern \nAfrica.",
