        "evidence_excerpt": "To the three magistrates seated upon the dais of the \ncourt, with the royal arms of England above their heads, \nthe pirate captain made his demand, prefacing his remarks \nwith nothing of the deference and respect which people \nusually showed when entering the presence of the \njustices, representatives of the majesty of the law which \ndwelled far across the tumbling wastes of water in distant \nWestminster.",
