        "evidence_excerpt": "Blackbeard sailed away south, and for some days \nnothing happened. Then it was noticed that Blackbeard \nand Hands were often in very secret talk; sometimes \nthey would be joined by Richards, and all three were very \nmysterious and resented any jesting inquiry on the part \nof the other pirates as to what they were talking about. \nA few days later the rumour went through the pirate \ncrew that they were going to Topsail Creek, a lonely \ninlet in the South Carolina coast, to clean and refit. As \nthey neared the creek Blackbeard, who seemed to be in \nliquor and was very hilarious, ordered the helmsman to \nsteer for the narrows at a place where, as the more sober \nof the crew recognized, there would be a considerable \nrisk of grounding. Sure enough the big ship did ground \non the sand there. Blackbeard knocked down the",
