        "evidence_excerpt": "Needless to say, these various outrages ended by \nstirring up hatred and in uniting all minds against the \npirate, and the traders, shipmasters, and better-class \nplanters resolved to submit to his oppression no longer. \nThey therefore, with as much secrecy as possible, sent a \ndeputation to Virginia to lay their grievances before the \nGovernor of that colony, and to solicit an armed force \nfrom the men-of-war lying in St James’s River.",
