        "evidence_excerpt": "of  peaceful  trade  which  had  been  pursued  for \ngenerations  by  Venetian  and  Genoese,  by  Spaniard \nand  Frenchman  ;  gone  also,  apparently  never  to \nreturn,  was  aU  sense  of  security  for  the  wretched \ndwellers  on  the  littoral  of  the  Mediterranean, \nwho  lived  in  daily,  and  particularly  in  nightly, \ndread  of  the  falcon  swoop  of  the  pirate  galleys.",
