          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e53211270a60a26aa03dc5168c85f7a9043def78664e708f0be035cea4a28c60",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Doria,  Grimani,  and  Capello  had  now  nearly \n200  ships  carrying  nearly  60,000  men.  Such \na  force,  in  all  ages,  has  been  considered  great. \nWilliam  the  Conqueror  conquered  Britain  with  a \nless  number ;  it  is  almost  half  the  total  of  the \npersonnel  of  the  British  fleet  in  the  preseiit  day \nwhich  has  to  defend  a  country  with  40,000,000 \ninhabitants,  and  all  this  force  had  been  raised, \narmed,  and  equipped  to  combat  with  a  Moslem \ncorsair.",
