      {
        "finding_id": "section-e898e8d33ce0fe618a2b",
        "file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean; the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton (Edward Hamilton)",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e53211270a60a26aa03dc5168c85f7a9043def78664e708f0be035cea4a28c60",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The  fact  of  the  intolerable  lot  of  the  common \nman  in  these  times  helps  us  to  understand  one \nthing  which  otherwise  would  be  an  insoluble \nproblem  :  which  was,  why  did  Christian  soldiers \nso  often  become  renegadoes  and  fight  for  the \ncorsairs  under  the  banner  of  those  who  were  the \nfiercest  and  most  irreconcilable  foes  of  themselves \nand  their  kindred  ?  The  life  of  the  common \nsoldier  or  sailor  did  not  offer  many  advantages  ;  it \nwas  generally  a  short  and  anything  but  a  merry \none,  and  the  thing  by  which  it  was  most  pro- \nfoundly affected  was  capture  by  the  corsairs.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
