        "evidence_excerpt": "On February 17th, he adds, “ Lé iy xumoured \nthat the Pandora will not go foreign wntil revon- \nmissioned, as she only wants four months for the \nexpiration of her three years, when she will be \npaid off, We are now waiting,” (he says,) “ for \nthe Champion and other oxperimental ships ol \nwar, 10 cruizo again by way of trial; but, I assure \nyou, the Pandora has completely lost all her good \nsailing qualities since her alteration, She holds a \ngood wind; but has not sufficient canvas; as ghe \nnow spreads loss on a wind, on that point of sail- \ning, by one hundred and fifty yards than before. \nTt therefore remains that*she hay not sufficient \npower 6n her, to force hor through the water, for \nshe ought to have more canvas on her now, na \na ship, than she had when she was a brig; because \nshe is deeper in the water, owing to tho groater \nsupply of sails, ropes, &c. and various other gear, \naccording io the establishment, We hyve had a \ntrial with the Brazen, and then wo Lound out our \ndefect.",
