        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The ambassador, when he rejoined his master, \nmust have been a proud man, as so well had he \nfulfilled his mission that he carried back with him \nto Algiers not only a gracious message, but the \ninsignia of the Sanjak, Scimitar Horse and Tam- \nbour, conferred upon that loyal Moslem Kheyr- \ned-Din Barbarossa, who, in the words of the \nPadishah, “abandoning a sterile independence, \nsought in all the bloody hazards of his life nought \nbut the glory of God and His Prophet.” ‘To us \nthis hyperbole, addressed to a pirate, seems merely \nridiculous, but in those days of fanaticism the \nbeliefs of men, both Christians and Moslems, are \nsomething which it is impossible for us to realise. \nOn either side the way of salvation was the path \nof conquest, and the man who was heretic to the \nfaith which you professed was rightly served if \nyou could cut him and his off from among the \ncongregation.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
