      {
        "finding_id": "section-390d6d6229a7bef742cf",
        "file": "india.history.resource.112019_112019_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-Wolves of the Mediterranean: The Grand Period of the Moslem Corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/india.history.resource.112019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "02bcc5c0781b01bf6c6e78ee0d5b8bfb31a02ea35b47565b888e171e88ef6ad9",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Aisa had a picked force of his uncle’s men, some \nseventeen hundred foot and six hundred horse, all \nseasoned and formidable veterans, inured to warfare \nby land and sea. On these of course he could rely \nto the death. The common folk of the town were \ninclined to make common cause with the corsairs in \nresistance to their hereditary enemy the Christians ; \nbut the magistrates and members of the council, \nthe grave and reverend signiors, held so conspicu- \nously aloof that Aisa was constrained into forcing \nthem to aid in the defence when he had time to \nattend to the matter. As Dragut was not actually \npresent at the siege it falls outside the scope of this \nchronicle; he was without the walls when the \nbesiegers arrived, but all that he could do, that he \ndid, With a body of his own men reinforced by",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
