        "evidence_excerpt": "With such skill and address did the corsair \nmanage his suit that he prevailed upon the Sultan \nto address a letter to Charles demanding the im- \nmediate return of the towns of Susa, Sfax, Monastir, \nand * Africa.” This, of course, meant war; as \nCharles immediately replied that these places were \ndependencies of the King of Tunis, and that that \nruler was under his special protection; further \nthat they were his by right of conquest ; finally \nthat the matter was no concern whatever of the \nSultan of Constantinople. 'The stern and imperious \nChristian Emperor was in no mood to brook inter- \nference, the more so that he discerned plainly that \nthough the demand was that of Soliman, the \nmover in the affair was none other than Dragut. \nHe therefore by way of a rider to his answer to \nthe Sultan informed that monarch that these places \nwhich he had taken on the coast of Africa had",
