      {
        "finding_id": "section-2d3290a5bfc5d49b962e",
        "file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Piracy in World History",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": null,
          "date": [
            "2021-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "It has also been argued that raiding and capturing practices existed \nprior to the Spanish arrival in the island world. Also, until the eighteenth \ncentury, neither colonial officers nor inhabitants of the islands applied \nthe term “Moro pirate\" (i.e. corsario moro or pirata moro). Instead, they \nwould write about enemigos mindanaos or about the harm caused by \nattacks carried out by indios mahometanos de Mindanao-77 Notwith- \nstanding the historical evidence for raids and captures on behalf of \nMuslim rulers, the way people remembered these incursions (piracy in \nthe Philippine south) was influenced by concurrent events of the past. \nThe double-biased term “Moro piracy\" refers to incursions of Muslim \nseafarers in the Christian communities in the Visayas, Luzon and parts \nof Northern Mindanao. Like other pre-modern piratical associations, the \nso-called Moro pirates were multi-ethnic and heteroogeneous. Raiders \noriginated from Maguindanao, Malanao, Lanun (Iranun), Sangil, Tausog, \nSamal, Badjao, and Balinguigui (from Sulu), occasionally to people from \nthe Moluccas or Borneo; moreover, Christian renegades and Chinese \nadventurers got involved on various occasions? Cesar A. Majul argued \nin this regard that piratical associations directed their blundering and \nraiding expeditions as often against territories that were not under Span- \nish colonial control and captured many coastal inhabitants that were",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
