          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "For the Nguyen Dynasty, the problem (or rather problems) of gidc was seri- \nous and existential. Several outbreaks of piracy, banditry, and rebellion \nin different parts of the country greatly weakened the Dynasty from the \nmid-nineteenth century. In the long run, the French incursions would \nprove to be the most serious threat to the regime, eventually leading to \nits downfall and the colonization of Vietnam in the 1880s. Nevertheless, \nthere were several other groups of pirates, bandits, rebels, and invaders \nthat caused serious trouble for the regime in different parts of Vietnam \nfrom the 1850s to the 1880s.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
