      {
        "finding_id": "section-3267b121c51f8dd65169",
        "file": "oapen-20.500.12657-53019_external_content_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Piracy in World History",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-53019",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": null,
          "date": [
            "2021-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8f3c05c7515e4753fdbf1e6c89ebadf36b36a537f0572450eb8246a8822c8366",
        "evidence_excerpt": "on commerce in the region.’ British officials sometimes described piracy \nas a universal crime, but they were reluctant to assert jurisdiction over \nforeigners, especially in Dutch spheres of influence, and they pressured local \npolities to aid in policing proximate seas.'? The complexities of jurisdiction \ncame out clearly in 1838, when the British ship Diana seized about 30 men \nfor an attack on a junk serving the valuable trade between Singapore and \nChina. Only about half the men brought before the British admiralty court \nin Singapore were sentenced, and when many of them claimed to be lawfully \nraiding on behalf of the Sultan of Sulu, the court wavered, declaring that \nthe case was evidently \"beyond the jurisdiction and powers of a Court of \nJustice.”° A few years later, British naval officers asked fewer questions \nwhen they were exhorted by the entrepreneurial James Brooke to attack \n“pirate” enclaves on the coast of Borneo.” Facing harsh criticism in London, \nofficials expressed uneasiness about incentives to label the victims of naval \nviolence \"pirates\" so that captains could claim head money under the Piracy \nAct of 1825. A commission that travelled to Singapore in 1854 to investigate \nwhether Dayaks targeted by British navy captains were in fact pirates found \nthat some Dayaks conducted piratical raids against local enemies but not \nagainst British ships — a conclusion that spoke volumes about the challenges \nof defining and punishing piracy under law.*?",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
