      {
        "finding_id": "section-7c56bc9b4d31e90ac048",
        "file": "7201c06d810a438109222b2d.txt",
        "title": "Piracy and captivity in the Mediterranean, 1550-1810 / edited by Mario Klarer",
        "url": "https://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb45536221m",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [],
          "date": [
            "2019"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "f5c6fb7cc1ffdcdcc478cf3a04d98c449f4a912bff93e05d623612b3d899a7c5",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Table des matières : Trading identities: Balthasar Sturmer's Verzeichnis der Reise (1558) and the making\n      of the European Barbary captivity narrative / Mario Klarer  ;  Unkind dealings: English\n      captivity narratives, commercial transformation, and the economy of unfree labor in\n      the early modern period / Daniel Vitkus  ; Ambivalences of recognition: the position\n      of the Barbary corsairs in early modern international law and international politics\n      / Walter Rech  ; \"Free, unfree, captive, slave\": António de Saldanha, a Late sixteenth-century\n      captive in Marrakesh / Peter Mark  ; \"Renegades\": converts to Islam in American Barbary\n      captivity narratives of the 1790s / Anna Diamantouli  ; Identity crises of homecomers\n      from the Barbary coast / Robert Spindler  ; \"Arab speculators\": states and ransom\n      slavery in the Western Sahara / Christine E. Sears  ; Michael Heberer: a prisoner\n      in the Ottoman Navy / Robert Rebitsch  ; Piracy, diplomacy, and cultural circulations\n      in the Mediterranean / Khalid Bekkaoui  ; Confraternity models in the \"redemption\n      of slaves\" in Europe: The Broederschap der alderheylighste Dryvuldigheyt of Bruges\n      (Brugge) and the Scuola della Santissima Trinità of Venice / Andrea Pelizza  ; Khayr\n      al-Din Barbarossa: clashing portraits of a Corsair-King / Diana de Armas Wilson  ;\n      A huguenot captive in Uthman Dey's court: Histoire chronologique du royaume de Tripoly\n      (1685) and its author / Gillian Weiss  ; Two Arabic accounts of captivity in Malta:\n      texts and contexts / Nabil Matar.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1685
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
