        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Afterward, whenever the pirates forgot their promise \nand were noisy at night, Cesar sent and ordered them \nto keep silent, and they instantly subsided, though with \nmuttered curses. After the first few days Cesar spoke \nto several of them, getting them to talk of their exploits \nand leading them to reveal their true natures, in which \ncraftiness, greed, and savagery mingled. Spartaco and \nMicio he particularly chose to talk to, and while he \nshowed his contempt for their trade and their manners, \nand never let them forget the social gulf which lay \nbetween them, he entered into many of their games and \ndiversions, got them to run and jump and throw balls \nwith him, and to walk with him about the island.",
