        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Within an hour the three galleys were under way to \nMiletus, crammed with men. The first contained Cesar \nand his friend Cinna, together with the freedman Gallo \nand the twoslaves, Cottaand Milo. Allexcept Cesar him- \nself showed great joy in at length finding themselves on \ntheir way to liberty again. They had been thirty-eight \ndays with the pirates, so hard a task had it been for Gallo \nand the other slaves of Cesar to collect the sum of fifty \ntalents. The property both of Cesar and his wife Cornelia \nhad been confiscated by Sulla, who was then tyrant at \nRome; but Cesar had many rich kinsmen and friends.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
