        "evidence_excerpt": "It would seem that these measures turned out to be \nsuccessful in the main. It is too much to suppose that \nsome of the pirates, finding life on shore pall upon them, \ndid not make their way to where the blue sea lay before \nthem, twinkling in the sunlight and beckoning with its \n‘innumerable smiles.’ But not for some generations \nwas the Mediterranean again afflicted by the scourge of \npiratical squadrons harrying, robbing, and murdering up \nand down the seaways and along the peaceful country-side.",
