        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "All about was the keen smell of the sea, filling the lads \nwith an exuberance as of wine. They pushed on through \nthe thinning mists, into which the great shafts of sun- \nlight seemed to pierce like wide, golden spear-heads, and \nin a little while they stood in some bushes looking down \non the shallow valley below them, two miles wide, over \nwhich the sea foamed at high tide. The sun was gaining \nthe mastery more and more over the mist-fiends which \nwere fleeing from his warmth and light, but the marsh \nwas still obscured in places. Suddenly Elphin bent and \npointed. ‘‘ Look!” hesaidin an excited whisper. ‘‘ It’s \na pirate boat! They’ve pushed up the creek in the mist \nand are landing! ”",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
