        "evidence_excerpt": "Both boys peered down, straining their eyes. Just \nbelow them, in a creek which ran into the marsh, was \none of the low, open galleys, captured specimens of which \nthey had often seen towed into the harbour of Rich- \nborough, or Rutupiz, where they lived, two miles away \non the other side of the marsh. But never had they seen \none filled with its crew of fierce, bearded pirates, as now \nthey saw them, each with a thick leather helmet on his",
