          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "But there had always been something of a hard reserve \nin Wulf’s manner when in the presence of strangers, as if \nhe felt that he was looked upon as of the breed of the \npirates whom men slaughtered or crucified, though, \nindeed, the Roman soldiers often suffered severely from \ndeath and wounds at the hands of the hardy and brave \nsea-rovers. Though Wulf and Elphin were great friends, \nWulf never spoke of what he wished to become when he \nwasaman. Elphin’s father had said he should join one of \nthe legions, as other Saxons and Angles had already done, \nthough they generally were sent to serve in other provinces \nthan Britain, to prevent treachery. Wulf never said \nwhether he was willing or unwilling to do this, though \nonce he told Elphin that he would prefer to go with him \nin the fleet—the sea was his place.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
