        "evidence_excerpt": "II \nTHE life which Elphin led now was a hard one, but its \nrough living was compensated for by the excitement \nwhich every day brought forth. The Seamew was one \nof a fleet of scout galleys which policed the seas from the \nSouth Foreland to the Wash. They had to be constantly \non the watch for any strange sail or rowing craft—for \noars were used as much as Sails in those days. They \nknew generally the ways over the sea by which the pirates",
