        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "came, and they cruised as near to this as wind and weather \npermitted them. As a rule the pirates waited for an \neast or anortheast wind ; then, issuing from the number- \nless creeks which lined the coasts from the Elbe to the \nZuyder Zee, and gathering in numbers as they went, they \nwould sail swiftly along the coast of Frisia and Batavia \n(Holland and Belgium). Finally they would separate at \nthe Rhine mouth, some making south to harry the shores \nof Gaul, others darting across to try their luck along the \nrich shores of Britain, whose country-side was studded \nwith wealthy towns and the fine villas of Romanized \nBritish nobles, officials, and merchants.",
