        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Where the straight Roman road, now known as the \nOld Kent Road, crossed the marshy lands of what we \nnow call Newington, a deputation from the citizens of \nLondinium met Theodosius and his legions and welcomed \nhim to their city. They told him how, from their thick, \nhigh walls, they had seen the murderous bands of Picts \nand Scots and pirates pass by, laden with spoil, and \nwith lines of wretched captives, and how the barbarians \nhad shaken their fists at the citizens, and shouted threats \nthat they would come back and burn and sack Londinium \nitself.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
