      {
        "finding_id": "section-4ef0983270be0ca4bd42",
        "file": "bookofpirates0000gilb_bookofpirates0000gilb_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The book of pirates",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/bookofpirates0000gilb",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Gilbert, Henry, 1868-1937",
          "date": [
            "1916-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Gradually, however, as Theodosius triumphed inland, \nhe could afford to give more men to make up the sea \ngarrisons, and then the tables began to be turned. The \nfleets of the British did not wait to be attacked, but \nunder the bold and skilful leadership of Elphin’s chief, \nVarro Rufinus, they sallied out and sought the Saxon \ngalleys, and now it was the pirates who often had to flee, \ntheir ships wrecked or sunk, and most of their men slain \nor wounded or taken prisoners.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/bookofpirates0000gilb",
          "source_file": "bookofpirates0000gilb_bookofpirates0000gilb_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 121820,
