        "evidence_excerpt": "As the years went by after the opening of the fifth \ncentury the raids of the pirates became fiercer and \nfiercer and the power of Rome declined more and more \nuntil at length, when every Roman soldier in the pro- \nvinces had been called back to Italy to save the Eternal \nCity from the Gothic hordes and Britain seemed to lie \ndefenceless at the mercy of her foes, the Saxon pirates \nbegan to look upon the country as a desirable one in \nwhich to settle. Continually after this did they come",
