        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The boats turned and rowed back to the creek where \nthe pirates had been hiding. A hurried council of war \nwas held, and it was decided that at midnight the \nbrigantine, with muffled oars, should be rowed into the \nbay where the galley lay, and an attempt be made to \noverpower the crew and seize the vessel. A spy was sent \non shore to learn what he could in the village of the \nMoriscoes, and then men saw to their weapons, feeling \nthe edges of their knives and sharpening them on their \nbelts. Extra knives were served out, for it would \nprobably be necessary to free and arm the galley slaves, \nwho would fight like furies against their masters. When \nthe spy returned he said :",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
