        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "When day dawned Sidi ben Muza looked upon the \nprize which he had captured and found that it exceeded \nall his expectations. It was a galley the possession of \nwhich would set him up as a respectable corsair, for it \nwas capable of holding four hundred men. Moreover, \nit was full of stores and arms, for it was one of the war \ngalleys of the King of Spain, and was a prize which even \nHajji Reis himself would have looked upon as a great \nacquisition.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
