      },
      {
        "finding_id": "section-b78d22ef2806f25a543f",
        "file": "bookofpirates0000gilb_bookofpirates0000gilb_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The book of pirates",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/bookofpirates0000gilb",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Gilbert, Henry, 1868-1937",
          "date": [
            "1916-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The men on the Spanish galleys were aware of the \npirate by now, but hesitated as to whether it was not \none of their own ships. Those moments of hesitation \nwere fateful. When the Spanish lieutenant, Don \nAmadeo, caught sight of the turbaned heads upon the \npoop he was no longer in doubt, but he hardly believed \nhis eyes when he saw the pirates making swiftly toward \nhim. Certainly his leader, Don Hurtado, and the main \npart of the men-at-arms were ashore on a private quarrel \nof the Duke of Alva, their master, but his force was still \na respectable one.",
