        },
        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Many were the proud hearts which broke under these \nintolerable conditions, many the tears, the agoniecs of \nseparation when mothers, daughters, sons, and fathers \nwere torn from each other’ Ss arms in the market-places. \nSome of the men, finding their captivity more than \nthey could bear, turned renegade, denied their religion \nand their race, and enrolled themselves as fighting-men \nunder a Moslem pirate. Others plotted to escape, but \nfew ever succeeded ; more often they were recaptured \nand subjected to horrible tortures ere they found relief \nin death.",
