        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Smyrna. Here, using the driving power of a strong \npersonality, and the name and influence of Khorkud, \nUruj at length succeeded in getting the ship, the equip- \nment, and the men, both sailors and slaves, necessary \nfor his purpose. The Basha of Smyrna, it is to be \nfeared, was not very enthusiastic about the matter; \nKhorkud had simply commanded his satrap to bear all \nexpenses, and whether he would ever see any return \nfor the five thousand ducats he had spent out of his \nprivate purse in carrying out Khorkud’s orders the Basha \nwas very doubtful. Certainly he got Uruj to promise \nto give him a share of all his captures, but, as the Basha \nreflected, Uruj was doubtless as much a rogue as any \nother pirate, and if he did not lose his galley would \nprobably keep no bargain that it was not to his own \nadvantage to keep.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
