        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The captain of the Galley of Naples had hoped that the \nwind would hold and thus keep his vessel going through \nthe water, but as the sun sank slowly into the waters \nof the west the breeze dropped. The red light touched \nthe faces of the combatants and bathed all the vessels \nin the colour of blood, and those passengers who ventured \nup from below to see how the fight was progressing went \nsick at heart to see this omen of disaster. Strive as the \npirates would, the swiftly falling darkness found them \nstill on their own galleys, having succeeded nowhere in \nmaking good a footing on the decks of the great sailing \nvessel.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
