        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "A few tents were pitched at the foot of the hills to \nshelter the Berber chieftains, but the remainder of the \nhost encamped in a semi-circle just out of range of the \nguns of the port. The seashore was left empty, but the \nChristian commander, casting his eyes to sea in the gather- \ning twilight, saw the galleys of the pirates lying off \nthe coast. Certainly his enemies were gathering closely \nabout him. Yet, as he looked up at the golden folds of \nthe Genoese flag, the brave commander resolved that, \nwhatever fate was to be his, he would never yield either \nto these land pirates, the Moslem raiders of the descrt, \nor to the sea robbers, the renegade Barbarossas.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
