        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "in which he made his way into Campeachy town. There, \nas he walked about, he saw the Spaniards making fires \nand drinking and rejoicing together. He asked a slave \nthe reason of this. “It is because a renowned pirate \nnamed Lolonais has been killed,” was the reply. “‘ Why \ndo they rejoice,” asked Lolonais, “seeing there are \nmany pirates to take his place?’’ ‘‘ He has harassed \nand injured them vastly,’’ answered the slave, “‘ and his \ncruelties against them have been such that the Spaniards \nwould rather choose to die or to sink fighting than to be \ntaken by him.”’ Which was very true, for he loved blood \nfor its own sake, and would torture his prisoners before \nhe slew them. Lolonais also heard that several of his \nmen were made captive by the Spaniards, and that these \nalso averred that he was dead.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
