        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "menacing the place, sent a ship to the relief of the town, \nwith ten guns and ninety men. It had been told the \ngovernor. that the pirates were commanded by the ill- \nfamed Lolonais. At this the governor swore passion- \nately, but he gave the captain of the relief ship a great \nnegro to serve for a hangman, and charged him “not to \nreturn into his presence without having totally destroyed \nthe pirates, except Lolonais, who was to be brought alive \nto the Havannah.”’",
