      {
        "finding_id": "section-074a69157cc25432aad0",
        "file": "bookofpirates0000gilb_bookofpirates0000gilb_djvu.txt",
        "title": "The book of pirates",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/bookofpirates0000gilb",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Gilbert, Henry, 1868-1937",
          "date": [
            "1916-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "1901bb10294e81f32d98c63cba8e03792d5ae5388c5c8aacfc5b904d67fab94d",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Next day, about noon, from the place where we had \nencamped outside the city we suddenly saw great clouds \nof smoke and flame rising from some of the chief buildings. \nMany of the Spaniards and some of our men did what \nthey could either to quench the flames, or, by blowing up \nsome houses and pulling down others, to stop the con- \nflagration but these efforts had little success. All the \nhouses of the city were built of cedar, very curious and \nmagnificent in appearance, and were adorned inside with \nhangings and pictures, and being of such material, many \nstreets were soon involved in the destroying element. \nThe fire increased so that before night the greater part of \nthe city was destroyed. I was very busy at that time \nat my duty of keeping an account of all booty that was \nbrought in, and I had little time to attend to much that \nwas said by the men who continually came and went from \nmy apartment in a villa where Captain Morgan had made \nhis headquarters. But I heard that some of the men \ncharged the Captain himself with having caused the city \nto be set on fire, which was a very foolish thing to say, \nseeing that by such means he stood to suffer as great loss \nin booty as any of them. I have no doubt it was as the \nCaptain alleged: that the Spaniards themelves had set \nfire to their town, permitting it rather to become a prey \nto the flames than to fall into the hands of pirates.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/bookofpirates0000gilb",
          "source_file": "bookofpirates0000gilb_bookofpirates0000gilb_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 411402,
          "end_char": 412812,
          "start_line": 10498,
          "end_line": 10522,
