        "evidence_excerpt": "“‘T’ll go ashore,” said the skipper with alacrity ; and \nnow that he saw he was not to be throttled or otherwise \nmade away with, he regained something of his spirits. \n“I wouldn’t be shipmates with such an unsociable swab \nas you, Avery, for all the gold in the sea. So this comes \no’ your refusing to drink with your Cap’n—while he was \ntrustin’ you, you was conspiring to turn pirate and \nseize the ship. If I ever ship another mate like you, \nAvery, who won't take his tot o’ rum every night like a \nman, well, [’lI——”",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
