        "evidence_excerpt": "Grumbling bitterly, the old man was turned out of his \ncabin, the door of which Avery locked, and in a few \nmoments Captain Dawson, the second mate, and eight \nof the imprisoned crew who would not join the pirates had \nclambered down into the long-boat of the Duchess, which \nwas still alongside, and amid the mocking messages of \nthe pirates they began their long pull back to land.",
