        "evidence_excerpt": "Avery found that his possession of the rich jewels was. \nlikely to become a burden, and that while he did not \ndare to sell them he was like to starve. Every day in his \npoor lodging he took them out, and the dazzling light \nand flashing beauty of them scared him, for it seemed \ninevitable that if he, a rough seaman, were found in \npossession of such wealth, he would be denounced as a \npirate. He therefore determined to endeavour to get \nrid of them through persons of respectable standing and \nappearance, whom rich merchants would trust, and with \nwhom they would deal fairly.",
