      {
        "finding_id": "section-277b66e9eb476cfc7c0c",
        "file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean; the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton (Edward Hamilton)",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e53211270a60a26aa03dc5168c85f7a9043def78664e708f0be035cea4a28c60",
        "evidence_excerpt": "his  forerunners,  and  the  ships  of  the  corsairs  had \nin  them  something  distinctive  in  that  they  were \npropelled  by  oars,  and  were  in  consequence,  to  a \ncertain  extent,  independent  of  the  weather.  Like \nthe  sailors  of  all  ages,  to  the  Sea-wolves  gales  and \nstorms  of  all  sorts  and  descriptions  were  abhorrent; \nand  in  consequence  they  had  a  well-marked  piracy \nseason,  which,  as  we  shall  see,  covered  the  spring \nand  summer,  while  they  carefully  avoided  the \ninclement  months  of  autumn  and  winter.",
