      {
        "finding_id": "section-0ffee08558a41ce74028",
        "file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean; the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton (Edward Hamilton)",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e53211270a60a26aa03dc5168c85f7a9043def78664e708f0be035cea4a28c60",
        "evidence_excerpt": "For  the  time  being  the  brothers  had  had  enough  of \nshore  enterprises,  and  confined  themselves  strictly \nto  their  piratical  business  at  sea,  which  prospered  so \nexceedingly  that  they  became  exceedingly  rich  and \ntheir  fame  and  power  increased  day  by  day.  As \ntime  went  on  and  the  wealth  of  the  brothers \nand  partners  increased,  there  entered  into  the \ncalculating  brain  of  Kheyr-ed-Din  the  idea  that  the \npayment  of  one-fifth  share  to  the  Sultan  of  Tunis \nwas  but  money  thrown  away.  Twenty  per  cent, \nwas  eating  into  the  profits  of  the  firm  in  an  un- \nwarrantable manner,  he  considered,  and  now  that \nthe  active  partners  therein  had  established  so  good \na  business  connection,  they  were  quite  strong \nenough  to  dispense  with  a  sleeping  partner.  Times \nhad  changed  for  the  better,  and  Kheyr-ed-Din  was \nanxious  to  take  full  advantage  of  the  fact ;  if \npossible  he  determined  to  seize  upon  and  hold  some \nport,  in  which,  not  only  would  they  be  exempt \nfrom  tribute,  but  also  in  which  he  and  his  brother \nUruj  should  be  the  supreme  arbiters  of  the  fate  of \nall  by  whom  it  might  be  frequented.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
