        "file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean; the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton (Edward Hamilton)",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e53211270a60a26aa03dc5168c85f7a9043def78664e708f0be035cea4a28c60",
        "evidence_excerpt": "century  the  Grand  Turk  was  in  every  sense  \"  far \naway  \"  from  the  struggUng  corsairs  on  the  httoral \nof  Northern  Africa,  and  was  a  sovereign  of  such \ngreat  and  mysterious  might  that  any  man  with  a \nless  fine  instinct  into  the  psychology  of  the  times \nin  which  he  lived  than  Kheyr-ed-Din  would  have \nhesitated  long  and  anxiously  before  addressing  him \ndirectly  ;  would  probably  in  the  end  not  have  done \nso  at  all.  But  desperate  diseases  require  desperate \nremedies,  and  the  politic  corsair  well  knew  that \neven  the  moral  support  of  such  an  one  as  the  Sultan \nof  Constantinople  was  worth  more  than  even \nmaterial  aid  from  a  Sultan  of  Tunis.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
