      {
        "finding_id": "section-bbb991fa33b71241a057",
        "file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean; the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton (Edward Hamilton)",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e53211270a60a26aa03dc5168c85f7a9043def78664e708f0be035cea4a28c60",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Freed  from  this  rival,  the  Mitylene  corsair  had \nnow  uncontested  supremacy  on  the  coast,  a  supre- \nmacy none  was  likely  to  contest  in  the  future,  as \nhe  brooked  no  opposition,  and  had  come  to  con- \nsider that  independent  piracy  in  the  Mediterranean \nwas  in  some  sort  an  infringement  of  the  rights  of \nhimself  and  his  brother.  One  of  the  most  salient \npeculiarities  of  the  corsairs  at  this  time  was  the \napparent  recklessness  with  which  they  assailed \nothers  who  were  participants  in  their  nefarious \nbusiness.  Self-interest  and  poUcy  would  seem,  to \nthe  observer  in  the  present  day,  to  have  dictated \nquite  a  different  course  of  action  ;  but  we  shall  see, \nwhen  we  come  to  deal  with  the  hfe-history  of \nKheyr-ed-Din,  that  this  infinitely  wiser  and  more \nintellectual  man  apparently  allowed  himself  to  be \nswayed  by  gusts  of  passion,  in  which  he  savagely \nmaltreated  those  with  whom  he  was  associated, \nand  from  whom  dangerous  hostihty  was  certainly \nto  be  feared  if  they  escaped  with  their  hves.  At \nthis  distance  of  time  it  is  impossible  to  gauge  the \nmotives  by  which  men  such  as  these  were  actuated, \nmore  particularly  in  the  case  of  Kheyr-ed-Din, \nwhose  character  was  a  blend  of  the  deepest  subtlety \nand  calculated  ferocity.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
          "source_file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
