      {
        "finding_id": "section-0854b4ba88d379cef32d",
        "file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean; the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton (Edward Hamilton)",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e53211270a60a26aa03dc5168c85f7a9043def78664e708f0be035cea4a28c60",
        "evidence_excerpt": "On  May  16th,  1530,  the  corsairs  once  again \nadvanced  to  the  assault.  By  this  time  the  walls \nhad  been  battered  until  a  practicable  breach  had \nbeen  formed,  and  over  this  swarmed  thirteen  hun- \ndred of  the  starkest  fighters  of  the  Mediterranean. \nIn  the  breach,  bareheaded,  his  armour  hacked \nand  dinted,  stood  the  undaunted  chieftain  of  the \nSpaniards :  over  his  head  floated  that  proud \nbanner  which  had  never  cast  its  shadow  on  a \nworthier  knight  of  Spain.  The  garrison,  worn \nto  a  shadow  by  their  hardships  and  their  hunger,",
        "years_in_scope": [],
