      {
        "finding_id": "section-3a926cd1977e7aaafc49",
        "file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean; the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton (Edward Hamilton)",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e53211270a60a26aa03dc5168c85f7a9043def78664e708f0be035cea4a28c60",
        "evidence_excerpt": "From  this  time  onward  until  1503  Andrea  was \nconstantly  employed  in  war,  and  made  for  himself \nsuch  a  reputation  that  in  this  year  the  Republic  of \nGenoa  requested  him  to  take  command  of  their \nnavy.  This  offer  he  refused,  as  he  said  that  he \nknew  nothing  about  the  sea.  They  pressed  him, \nsaying  that  to  a  man  of  his  genius  nothing  was \nimpossible,  and  in  the  end  he  gave  a  somewhat \nreluctant  consent.  He  soon  proved  his  com- \npetence in  his  new  sphere  of  activity,  as  his  first \nact  was  to  capture  the  Fort  of  the  Lantern,  in  the \nneighbourhood  of  Genoa,  which  was  then  held  by \nthe  French  for  Louis  XII.  The  Republic  con- \nfirmed his  appointment  as  General  of  the  Galleys \nwith  many  compliments,  and  he  put  to  sea  and  cap- \ntured three  of  the  war-galleys  of  the  corsairs^  also \ntwo  Turkish  ships  laden  with  valuable  merchandise. \nHe  fitted  out  the  galleys  for  his  own  service,  sold \nthe  merchantmen,  and  made  an  immense  sum  of \nmoney.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
          "source_file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
