      {
        "finding_id": "section-b586e8444880f1e0b9ad",
        "file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean; the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton (Edward Hamilton)",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e53211270a60a26aa03dc5168c85f7a9043def78664e708f0be035cea4a28c60",
        "evidence_excerpt": "That  warrior,  nothing  disconcerted,  pursued  his \nway  to  the  island  of  Zante,  where  he  fell  in  with \na  Turkish  \"  flota,\"  under  the  command  of  the \nBashas  Zay  and  Himeral.  To  these  officers  of \nthe  Grand  Turk  Barbarossa  used  most  injurious \nlanguage,  bitterly  reproaching  them  with  not \nhaving  sought  out  and  destroyed  Andrea  Doria, \nwhich  he  declared  they  ought  to  and  should  have \ndone.  This  is  yet  another  instance  of  the  extra- \nordinary character  of  the  man.  These  persons \nwere  the  highest  officers  in  the  fleet  of  the \nOttoman  Empire  ;  it  was  more  than  possible  that \nthey  would  be  placed  under  the  command  of \nBarbarossa  as  soon  as  his  new  position  as  Admiral- \nissimo  was  adjusted  at  Constantinople  ;  and  yet, \nin  spite  of  these  facts,  the  corsair  had  taken  the \nvery  first  opportunity  which  presented  itself  grossly \nto  insult  these  men.  It  is  true,  as  we  shall  See, \nthat  his  injurious  words  came  home  to  roost  in  the \nfuture;  but  arrogant.  Conquering,  contemptuous, \nBarbarossa  seems  to  have  shouldered  his  way \nthrough  life,  fearing  none  and  feared  by  all.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
