      {
        "finding_id": "section-62cc2088545140926ecb",
        "file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean; the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton (Edward Hamilton)",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e53211270a60a26aa03dc5168c85f7a9043def78664e708f0be035cea4a28c60",
        "evidence_excerpt": "God,  each  retired  to  his  post  to  die  on  the  bed \nof  honour  with  arms  in  his  hand.\"  Those  among \nthe  Knights  who  were  too  severely  wounded  or \ntoo  ill  to  stand  caused  chairs  to  be  carried  to  the \nbreach  in  which  they  seated  themselves  and  awaited \nthe  assault.  For  four  hours  did  these  indomitable \nmen  withstand  the  might  of  a  host  innumerable : \nat  the  conclusion  of  this  period  there  remained \nalive  but  sixty  of  the  garrison.  Mustafa  ceased \nthe  assault  for  a  few  moments  only  to  replace  the \nstorming  party  by  fresh  troops,  and  then  the  end \ncame.  Almost  the  last  to  fall  were  the  Chevalier \nLamirande  and  the  veteran  Bailli  of  Negropont, \nand  when  the  crescent  banner  was  planted  on  the \nwalls  there  remained  alive  not  one  of  those  de- \nfenders who  had  held  the  fort.  Several  of  Dragut's \nofficers  ran  to  his  tent  and  announced  the  taking \nof  St.  Elmo.  The  great  captain  was  in  his  last \nextremity  and  unable  to  speak,  \"  He,  however, \nmanifested  his  joy  by  several  signs,  and,  raising  his \neyes  to  heaven  as  if  in  thankfulness  for  its  mercies, \nimmediately  expired :  a  captain  of  rare  valour  and \neven  abundantly  more  humane  than  are  ordinarily \nthese  corsairs.\"",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
