      {
        "finding_id": "section-cd62927583275b368d19",
        "file": "cu31924087978445_cu31924087978445_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean; the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/cu31924087978445",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, E. Hamilton (Edward Hamilton)",
          "date": [
            "1910-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e53211270a60a26aa03dc5168c85f7a9043def78664e708f0be035cea4a28c60",
        "evidence_excerpt": "There  were  three  principal  conspirators — the \nAlcaid  Bengabara,  General  of  the  Cavalry,  the \nAlcaid  Botaybo,  and  the  Alcaid  Alcadaar.  Ali, \nhowever,  was  too  shrewd  a  man  to  move  until  he \nhad  satisfied  himself  by  reports  from  his  own  ad- \nherents ;  he,  therefore,  awaited  the  result  of  in- \nvestigations made  by  spies  from  Algiers.  At  last, \nin  the  beginning  of  the  year  1569,  when  the  offers \nfrom  the  Alcaids  had  been  three  times  renewed \nand  the  Basha  was  assured  that  the  people  in \nTunis  were  sincere  in  their  offer  to  him  of  the \nsovereignty  of  the  kingdom — which  they  begged \nhim  to  conquer  and  hold  in  the  name  of  the \nOttoman  Empire — the  ex-galley-slave  no  longer \nhesitated.  He  left  Algiers  in  the  month  of \nOctober,  leaving  that  city  in  charge  of  one  Mami \nCorso,  a  fellow  renegado.  Unlike  Dragut,  who \nwould  have  gone  by  sea,  he  set  out  by  land  with \nsome  five  thousand  corsairs  and  renegadoes.  On \nthe  way  he  was  reinforced  by  some  six  thousand \ncavalry  of  the  vvdld  tribes  of  the  hinterland,  then",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
