        "evidence_excerpt": "On the 13th, being in the latitude of Cadiz, we received \nintelligence that a fleet of men of war and merchantmen, bound \nfrom thence to Lima, were ready to fail; we therefore cleared \nfor action. On the 14th we fpoke two Portuguefe men of \nwar, the St. Sebaflian and Principe Reale; the latter bearing the \nflag of the Marquis de Neyfa: they were on their paflage from \nPalermo to Liflxm. On the 29th we fell in with the Balloon, \nPortuguefe brig, commanded by an emigrant, the Count de \nBlofville, with an Algerine corfair of 22 guns in company, \nwhich he had lately captured. On the 31ft a fail was fuppofed \nto be defcried by the man at the maft head; but as the haze \ncleared up it proved to be a whale fpouting up water.",
