        "evidence_excerpt": "* We are now (June 7th) at Leghorn, I am \nmuch pleased with this place, it being a clean, \npleasant little town. There is, on the mole, a very \nbeautiful monument of four gigantic bronze statues, \naround an immense marble one, representing the \nGrand Duke’s son, who, they say, was put to \ndeath for breaking quarantine, The story is this: \n—A pirate had very much annoyed the vessels \nbelowigiig to the Duke's dominions, and nobody \nwould engage with him. The Duke’s son, being \n‘a brave man, manned a boat, and went out to mect",
