        "evidence_excerpt": "“ From Penang we went the best of our way \nto Malacca, passing through the straits of” Callam, \na most notorious place for pirates; in fact, all \nalong the Malay coast it is tlfe same. It so \nhappened we were obliged 1o anchor here, when \nabout midway, the wind failing and the tide \nagainst wsi—at about eight o’clock that night, \nbehold two proas were dropping down with the \ntide. Now, you must know, that few alupa ever \ngo through this place, on account of thesé very \nproas, which are manned by fifty or sixty men \nin cach, and acmed with a long gun in the bow, \n‘on 4 swivel. Immediately wo perceived them",
